          "thm-existence-and-uniqueness-of-a-maximal-ode-solution",
          "thm-ftc-second-part",
          "thm-continuous-implies-integrable",
          "thm-monotonicity-of-the-integral"
        ],
        "dependency_level": 2,
        "statement": "Let $H$, $K$, the range provider, $L,M$, and the initial box $Y_0=X_0\\times\\{I_d\\}\\times\\Theta$ satisfy [[def-verified-flow-variational-range-oracle]] and [[alg-validated-euler-flow-and-monodromy-enclosure]]. If that procedure returns success with boxes $Q_0,\\ldots,Q_{N-1}$ and $Y_N$, then for every $(x_0,\\theta)\\in X_0\\times\\Theta$ the unique solution of $y'=H(y)$ from $(x_0,I_d,\\theta)$ exists through time $1$, its trajectory on $[n/N,(n+1)/N]$ lies in $Q_n$, and its terminal state lies in $Y_N$. Consequently the endpoint state encloses $\\phi_\\theta(x_0)$ and the matrix block encloses $D_x\\phi_\\theta(x_0)$.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "lem-phase-border-implies-periodic-bvp-linearization-bounded-inverse",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "title": "A transverse phase border makes the periodic BVP linearization boundedly invertible",
        "deps": [
          "def-phase-bordered-periodic-orbit-bvp",
          "lem-phase-bordered-shooting-jacobian-invertibility",
          "def-linearized-two-point-bvp-operator-and-conditioning",
          "lem-c1-euclidean-maximal-flow-with-c2-upgrade",
          "thm-gronwall-integral-inequality",
          "thm-picard-lindelof-local-existence-and-uniqueness",
          "thm-existence-and-uniqueness-of-a-maximal-ode-solution",
          "thm-ftc-second-part",
          "thm-chain-rule-for-total-derivatives",
          "thm-norm-inequality-for-the-vector-valued-integral",
          "thm-continuous-implies-integrable",
          "thm-monotonicity-of-the-integral"
        ],
        "dependency_level": 3,
        "statement": "Let $u_*(s)=(\\gamma(Ts),T)$, $0\\le s\\le1$, be the augmented solution from [[def-phase-bordered-periodic-orbit-bvp]] for a nonconstant $C^2$ autonomous periodic orbit of period $T>0$. Assume its phase multiplier $1$ is algebraically simple and its affine phase covector $c$ satisfies $c^\\top f(\\gamma(0))\\ne0$. For the continuous linearized BVP operator $\\mathcal L:X\\to Z$ of [[def-linearized-two-point-bvp-operator-and-conditioning]], define\n$$ A(s)=D\\widetilde f(u_*(s)),\\quad a_0=\\sup_{0\\le s\\le1}\\|A(s)\\|_2, \\quad B_2=D_2B(u_*(0),u_*(1)),\\quad K_J\\ge\\|J^{-1}\\|_{2\\to2}, $$\nwhere $J=\\begin{bmatrix}M-I&f(\\gamma(0))\\\\c^\\top&0\\end{bmatrix}$ and $M=D\\phi_T(\\gamma(0))$. Put $E=e^{a_0}$ and\n$$ K_{\\mathcal L}:=(1+a_0)\\left[E K_J(1+\\|B_2\\|_2E)+E\\right]+1. $$\nThen $\\mathcal L$ is bijective and $\\|\\mathcal L^{-1}\\|_{Z\\to X}\\le K_{\\mathcal L}$, with the spaces and norms defined in [[def-linearized-two-point-bvp-operator-and-conditioning]]. All constants are finite and explicit once the stated coefficient and shooting-inverse bounds are supplied.\n\n"
      },
