      {
        "id": "thm-periodic-shooting-residual-to-orbit-error-budget",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "title": "A certified shooting residual gives an explicit local periodic-orbit error bound",
        "deps": [
          "def-phase-bordered-periodic-orbit-bvp",
          "def-validated-periodic-shooting-jet-enclosure",
          "lem-phase-bordered-shooting-jacobian-invertibility",
          "thm-gronwall-integral-inequality",
          "thm-chain-rule-for-total-derivatives",
          "thm-c2-ode-flow-on-common-tube",
          "thm-ftc-second-part",
          "thm-norm-inequality-for-the-vector-valued-integral",
          "thm-continuous-implies-integrable",
          "thm-monotonicity-of-the-integral"
        ],
        "dependency_level": 6,
        "statement": "Let $z_*=(x_*,T_*)$ be a phase-fixed nonconstant periodic orbit, let $G$ be its phase-bordered shooting residual, and suppose $DG(z_*)$ is invertible with $\\|DG(z_*)^{-1}\\|_2\\le K_J$. Let a convex validated domain contain the segment from $z_*$ to a candidate $z=(x,T)$, with $\\|z-z_*\\|_2\\le r$, and suppose $DG$ is $L_J$-Lipschitz there and $K_JL_Jr\\le1$. If a validated residual box $R$ contains $G(z)$ and $\\epsilon\\ge\\sup_{v\\in R}\\|v\\|_2$, then\n$$ \\|z-z_*\\|_2\\le2K_J\\epsilon. $$\nIf both scaled trajectories $\\phi_{Ts}(x)$ and $\\phi_{T_*s}(x_*)$ exist and lie in one convex state tube $K\\subset U$ for every $s\\in[0,1]$, with $\\|Df\\|_2\\le L_f$ and $\\|f\\|_2\\le M_f$ on $K$ and $0<T,T_*\\le T_+$, then they satisfy\n$$ \\sup_{0\\le s\\le1}\\|\\phi_{Ts}(x)-\\phi_{T_*s}(x_*)\\|_2 \\le 2K_J e^{T_+L_f}(1+M_f)\\epsilon. $$\nThe residual box may be taken from [[def-validated-periodic-shooting-jet-enclosure]]. A residual without the stated neighborhood, inverse, and derivative bounds gives no orbit-error conclusion."
      },
